d Europeans in 1967, and the always redoubtable German, " [:a {:href "/athletes/58341"} "Wilfried Dietrich"] ". Form held as those three made the finals. Medved had defeated Duraliev by decision in round three and had thrown Dietrich in round five, which gave him the gold medal. Duraliev threw Dietrich in the final match to secure the silver medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Medved would return in 1972 and win a third consecutive gold medal, this time as a super-heavyweight, with Duraliev again finishing second to him. This was Dietrich’s fifth Olympic medal, an Olympic record for wrestling that was not matched until 2024 by Cuban " [:a {:href "/athletes/107601"} "Mijaín López"] ". Dietrich would compete again in 1972, in both styles, but would not win another medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {} "Bad Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60505"} "Aliaksandr Miadved"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/57391"} "Osman Duraliev"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BUL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BUL.png"}] "BUL"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "9"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58341"} "Wilfried Dietrich"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "h